  "problem": "The sidebar reused one active native select as its session source, coupled expansion with workspace selection, and saved selection using a mutable selected-workspace variable. It had no independent workspace catalogue. Earlier acceptance switched active workspaces rather than keeping multiple groups expanded.",
  "change": "C++ serves a read-only catalogue for an explicit registered workspace after validating browser access, without changing its selected workspace/cookie or issuing a browser lease. Session lists and expansion state are keyed by workspace; selected rows/actions are scoped by workspace plus session ID. Controllers capture their workspace for saves/posts, suppress retired responses, and read scoped catalogues. Clicking a session in another workspace uses the normal native selection handler and preserves an already-restored inspected run.",
